WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:08.186
Week 3: Objects, Gender, and the Classroom. identify people and objects ask what something is follow basic instructions

2
00:00:08.186 --> 00:00:29.484
Read for the situation. En el aula hay veinte sillas y diez mesas. La profesora abre un libro y escribe una pregunta. Los estudiantes buscan la respuesta en sus cuadernos. There are twenty chairs and ten tables in the classroom. The teacher opens a book and writes a question. The students look for the answer in their notebooks.

3
00:00:29.484 --> 00:00:38.054
Read again for evidence. Identify who acts, what changes, when it happens, and which words establish the relationship between events.

4
00:00:38.054 --> 00:00:44.405
Reading activities. Reading activity 5; Reading activity 6; Reading activity 7

5
00:00:44.405 --> 00:00:52.186
Retell. Without looking back, give the main idea, three supporting details, and one reasonable inference in Spanish.

6
00:00:52.186 --> 00:01:16.247
Model language. En el aula hay veinte sillas. — In the classroom there are twenty chairs. También hay diez mesas. — There are also ten tables. La profesora escribe una pregunta. — The teacher writes a question. Los estudiantes buscan la respuesta. — The students look for the answer. La encuentran en la página diez. — They find it on page ten.

7
00:01:16.247 --> 00:01:25.995
Check your readiness. Explain the core idea. Produce an original example. Complete the section assessment at 85% or higher.
